# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages, for the routes with no prerendered file of
# their own: the detail pages (/admin/students/s0, /tutor/classes/c0) and 404s.
# Static assets and prerendered routes are matched first, so every public page
# still serves its own HTML with its own link-preview tags.
#
# The destination must be /index.html. Pages strips .html from a destination and
# turns it into a 308, so pointing this at Nuxt's empty /200.html shell instead
# resolves to /200, which then 308s to itself: an infinite loop on every URL,
# static assets included. /index.html is the one destination Pages special-cases.
#
# Cost of that: index.html now holds the prerendered marketing homepage, so a
# deep link straight to a portal detail screen paints the homepage for a frame
# before the router swaps it out. Only hard loads hit this, never in-app clicks.
/*    /index.html   200
